  "approach": "Teach un, una, unos and unas, the plural meaning \"some\" or \"about\", and the two places Spanish leaves the indefinite article out where English uses \"a\": a bare profession after ser, and before otro.",
  "coverage": [
    "un (masc.), una (fem.): a, an",
    "unos, unas: some, a few; with numbers, about: unos veinte",
    "Tengo unas amigas en Chile. (I have some friends in Chile.)",
    "Ser + profession alone takes no article: Es profesor. Soy médica.",
    "Add un or una when the profession is described: Es un profesor excelente",
    "No un before otro: otro café (another coffee), never un otro café"
  ],
